! Bmad translation of Genesis4's benchmark/Benchmark1-SASE/Aramis.lat, the lattice the
! comparison tiers run. Its code is identical to examples/aramis.bmad, which is the copy
! the examples call, and the two are kept that way on purpose: the tiers and the examples
! measure the same line.
!
! e_tot is the reference energy and the driver derives gamma0 from it. Genesis4's
! benchmark value 11357.82 is encoded as an expression in Bmad's own rest mass.
!
! Genesis4's quadrupole k1 = 2 m^-2 is the geometric strength at the reference energy
! and Bmad's k1 means the same. The chromatic behavior differs at the model level:
! Genesis scales the focusing per particle by gamma0/gammaz (TrackBeam.cpp:26,69), Bmad by
! p0/p. The two differ by ~4e-9 relative at this energy, quantified in the benchmark README.

no_digested
parameter[geometry] = open
parameter[particle] = electron
parameter[e_tot] = 11357.82 * m_electron

! The matched periodic Twiss of this FODO cell at this energy (Genesis4's zmatch values,
! the same numbers the benchmark namelists carry). The FEL walk itself never reads
! lattice Twiss. Imports do, since init_beam_distribution matches the bunch it generates
! to these.
beginning[beta_a] = 8.53711
beginning[alpha_a] = -0.703306
beginning[beta_b] = 17.3899
beginning[alpha_b] = 1.40348

! The FEL element: a real wiggler tracked by fel_averaged, one of Bmad's two FEL methods.
! The FEL parameters derive from the attributes. aw = c*b_max/(k_u*m_e c^2) for a helical
! device in the rms convention, so b_max below encodes aw = 0.84853 exactly as an
! expression in Bmad's own constants. Helicity comes from field_calc and the period from
! l_period.
UND: wiggler, l = 3.99, l_period = 0.015, field_calc = helical_model, &
     b_max = 0.84853 * (twopi / 0.015) * m_electron / c_light, &
     tracking_method = fel_averaged, ds_step = 0.045
D1: drift, l = 0.44
D2: drift, l = 0.24
QF: quadrupole, l = 0.08, k1 = 2.0
QD: quadrupole, l = 0.08, k1 = -2.0

FODO: line = (UND, D1, QF, D2, UND, D1, QD, D2)
ARAMIS: line = (6*FODO)

use, ARAMIS
